<!-- DQ HISTORY & OVERVIEW -->
<section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="about-dq-h2">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <span class="section-kicker center" style="display:block;">Est. 1940 · The Original American Soft Serve</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" id="about-dq-h2">About the Dairy Queen Menu</h2>
    <p>Dairy Queen has been serving America since June 22, 1940, when the first DQ opened in Joliet, Illinois. What started as a single soft-serve ice cream stand has grown into one of the world's largest fast-food chains — 7,700+ locations in more than 20 countries, all united by the same creamy soft serve that made DQ famous. This is your complete <a href="/#full-menu">Dairy Queen menu with 2026 prices</a>, every Blizzard flavor, and every calorie count in one place.</p>
    <p>The modern DQ menu divides into two main tracks: <strong>DQ Grill &amp; Chill</strong> locations serve the full food and treats lineup — Stackburgers, Chicken Strip Baskets, breakfast (at select times), and all frozen treats. <strong>DQ Treat</strong> locations focus on Blizzards, cones, sundaes, shakes, and DQ Cakes. Most mall-based DQs are Treat locations. If you're planning to order food, verify your local DQ is a Grill &amp; Chill before you go.</p>
    <p>Prices on this site are national averages for 2026. Individual franchise locations may price slightly above or below the averages listed. The <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> remains the best value for a complete meal. For pure dessert value, the Mini Blizzard at $3.49 is hard to beat. For celebrations, <a href="/categories/dq-cakes">DQ Cakes</a> start at $22.99 and are fully customizable with 48-hour advance ordering.</p>
  </div>
</section>

